From 8e2f140c25a92ebd43aa51374f406149911f8266 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iori Yanokura <ab.ioryz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:51:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] hw/gpio: Add Renesas RA I/O ports and pin function select
 (PFS)

Model PORT0..9 (PCNTR1..4), the PmnPFS registers and PMISC. The 16-bit
aliases of these registers do not follow little-endian byte lanes (the
alias at +0 of PCNTR1 is PODR, which is bits 31:16 of the 32-bit view),
so accesses are decoded by width. PODR/PDR are shared between the port
and PFS views, and every pin exposes its output level as a GPIO line.
---
 hw/gpio/Kconfig                     |   3 +
 hw/gpio/meson.build                 |   2 +
 hw/gpio/renesas_ra_ioport.c         | 279 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/hw/gpio/renesas_ra_ioport.h |  42 +++++
 4 files changed, 326 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/gpio/renesas_ra_ioport.c
 create mode 100644 include/hw/gpio/renesas_ra_ioport.h

